# The working directory this repo lives in also holds material that must
# never be committed: client documents, an Oracle wallet (private keys),
# spreadsheets and ad-hoc screenshots. Rather than blacklisting each
# sensitive item individually -- where missing one is silent and
# permanent -- this ignores EVERYTHING by default and whitelists only the
# paths that genuinely belong to the repo: the GitHub Actions workflows,
# the INSIGHT_oracle_26node_apex_python_container project folder,
# INSIGHT_app.html (tracked so CI can diff it against web/index.html and
# catch the two copies drifting -- see ci.yml), and INSIGHT_addons/ (the
# COA setup tools + discovery/product-mapping workbook -- real project
# artifacts, not scratch files). Anything new added to the working
# directory is untracked unless explicitly whitelisted below.
#
# Deliberately NOT tracked, though both live in this folder:
#   - INSIGHT_All_Clients_Roster.xlsx -- the manual client-tracking roster.
#     Even with placeholder rows it carries named contacts, titles and
#     email addresses in a column layout built for real engagements. This
#     repo is public and git history is permanent, so a future update
#     containing real client data would be published irreversibly. Keep it
#     local.
#   - Screenshots. Ad-hoc, dated, and never a build input.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/.github/
!/INSIGHT_oracle_26node_apex_python_container/
!/INSIGHT_app.html
!/INSIGHT_addons/
Screenshot*.png
*/Screenshot*.png
